A sphere's core: its name, summary, other names, timeline and drawer
outline with a few items each. Wording from
docs/superpowers/probes/2026-10-22-spheres.md, "Recommended prompt text"
(a): the flat shape (drawers, then items naming their drawer by title),
which the probe found complete 12 of 12 times where a nested one broke.

`label` names the template for the model ("religion (a faith or church)"),
`template` is the template ("sphere" for other) and `agent` its flag.
`known` is a promoted thing's own facts; `part_of` is `[(heading, facts)]`
for the entries already part of it. The Connections blocks are
create-thing's: `mentions` `[(lead, text)]`, `about` `[(heading, facts)]`,
`named` `[(written, heading, facts)]`. `start_drawers` is `[(type,
title)]`, the template's drawers less people, events and branches, and
`types` `[(type, help)]` the drawer types the reply may write.
-#}
